.TH QUANUXCTL-ENGINE 1 "March 2026" "QuanuX" "QuanuX Control Manual"
.SH NAME
quanuxctl-engine \- QuanuX Edge Engine Tuning & Execution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanuxctl engine
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quanuxctl engine
bridges the ephemeral infrastructure state to the QuanuX configuration management layout. It is securely responsible for OS/Kernel deterministic tuning, CNATS cluster deployment, and the strict lifecycle of the native Annex C++ decoder processes.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B tune \fB--target [do|gcp]\fR
Invokes kernel and OS tuning playbooks for the designated cloud architecture natively.
For GCP targets, this intentionally disables THP in favor of enforcing Static Hugepages, isolates CPU assignments via grub, and injects raw network buffer parameters for low-latency transmission protocols.
.TP
.B start \fB--target [do|gcp]\fR
Initializes CNATS JetStream, starts the parent Annex ingestion sub-services, and securely compiles the Omega C++ Decoder natively on the target hardware payload footprint.
.TP
.B setup-topology \fB--target [do|gcp]\fR
Configures the core JetStream QUANUX_INGEST stream.
Provisions the Stream with 50GB file-backed storage limits on the live cluster.
Attaches the ANNEX_PROCESSOR and ALEPH_OBSERVER consumers configured for Durable Pull requests with Explicit ACKs, enabling line-rate ingestion loops safely.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B QUANUX_TARGET
Determines the tfstate dynamic inventory path mapping for secure state extraction.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on successful Ansible playbook execution string. Returns 1 on task or subsystem failure.
